{"content":[{"c":["ELAH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Esau’s descendant and a chief of Edom (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.36.41","r":"Gen.36.41","rawR":"Gen.36.41","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.36.41","value":"Gen.36.41"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 36:41"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.1.52","r":"1Chr.1.52","rawR":"1Chr.1.52","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.1.52","value":"1Chr.1.52"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 1:52"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. KJV rendering of Ela, Shimei’s father, in ",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.4.18","r":"1Kgs.4.18","rawR":"1Kgs.4.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.4.18","value":"1Kgs.4.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kings 4:18"},". ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Ela_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Ela_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Ela_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Ela"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. Baasha’s son and fourth king of Israel. Elah reigned for only two years (886–885 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},"). While in a drunken stupor, he was murdered by one of his generals (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.16.8-14","r":"1Kgs.16.8-14","rawR":"1Kgs.16.8-14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.16.8-14","value":"1Kgs.16.8-14"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 16:8-14"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["4. Father of Hoshea, the last king of the northern kingdom of Israel (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.15.30","r":"2Kgs.15.30","rawR":"2Kgs.15.30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.15.30","value":"2Kgs.15.30"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 15:30"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.17.1","r":"2Kgs.17.1","rawR":"2Kgs.17.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.17.1","value":"2Kgs.17.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"17:1"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.18.1,9","r":"2Kgs.18.1,9","rawR":"2Kgs.18.1,9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.18.1,9","value":"2Kgs.18.1,9"}],"t":"ref","v":"18:1, 9"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["5. Caleb’s second son and father of Kenaz (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.4.15","r":"1Chr.4.15","rawR":"1Chr.4.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.4.15","value":"1Chr.4.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 4:15"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["6. Uzzi’s son, descendant of Benjamin (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.9.8","r":"1Chr.9.8","rawR":"1Chr.9.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.9.8","value":"1Chr.9.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 9:8"},"). Elah was among the first to resettle in Jerusalem after the Babylonian exile. He is not mentioned in the parallel list of ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.11.1-36","r":"Neh.11.1-36","rawR":"Neh.11.1-36","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.11.1-36","value":"Neh.11.1-36"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nehemiah 11"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Elah","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 36:41","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.36.41","rawQueryValue":"Gen.36.41","sourceRefExact":"Gen.36.41"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 1:52","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.1.52","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.1.52","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.1.52"},{"anchorText":"1 Kings 4:18","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.4.18","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.4.18","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.4.18"},{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 16:8-14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.16.8-14","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.16.8-14","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.16.8-14"},{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 15:30","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.15.30","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.15.30","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.15.30"},{"anchorText":"17:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.17.1","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.17.1","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.17.1"},{"anchorText":"18:1, 9","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.18.1,9","rawQueryVal